# Player game manual

Authoritative player handbook lives under **`docs/manual/`**. GDD/TDD/UI/AI SPECs remain the sole sources of truth for behavior; the manual must never contradict them. On conflict, fix the manual.

Normative writing conventions: [`docs/manual/STYLE_GUIDE.md`](../../docs/manual/STYLE_GUIDE.md). ToC: [`docs/manual/index.md`](../../docs/manual/index.md). Updater workflow: `.cursor/skills/update-game-manual/SKILL.md`.

## Player UX / gameplay impact (authoritative trigger)

Update the manual whenever work changes what the player can **do**, **see**, or be **told** — including map affordances, screen copy, order availability, visible outcomes, mechanic teachability, and decision-support cues — even when the change is “only UI” or “only a bug fix.”

**Exempt (manual update not required):** ctdev-only surfaces (`SPEC/program/ctdev-app.md` and siblings), pure internal refactors with **zero** player-visible delta, tooling/CI, and performance work that preserves identical player-visible behavior.

When exempt, record a one-line **manual non-update justification** in the issue or PR body.

## Lifecycle obligations (all agents)

| Phase | Skill / gate | Requirement |
|-------|----------------|-------------|
| Issue filing | `create-github-issue`, `plan-feature` | If player UX/gameplay is impacted: name target manual chapter(s), add a **Manual follow-up** subtask, and include a testable AC for `docs/manual/` update (or explicit justified non-update). |
| Implementation | `implement-github-issue` | Run **`update-game-manual`** before opening/updating the PR when the issue touches player UX/gameplay. |
| PR review | `review-pr` | Player-impacting PRs must update affected manual chapters **or** justify non-update in the PR body. |
| Verification | `verify-github-issue` | Check manual AC / chapter updates on merged `dev` when the issue is player-facing. When chapters were updated, audit them for STYLE_GUIDE conformance and SPEC-accurate instructions/UI refs (same two checks as `review-game-manual-agent`). |

Identify affected chapters by **exact string match** of changed SPEC paths against each chapter’s `## Sources` bullets (see style guide). When no Sources match yet, use the ToC coverage map in `docs/manual/index.md`.

## When this rule applies (file globs)

- Editing any file under `docs/manual/**`.
- Editing `SPEC/game/**`, `SPEC/ui/**`, or an allowlisted `SPEC/program/` file (below).

## Required-review trigger (PRs)

A PR **must** review affected manual chapters (update them, or explicitly justify no update) when it modifies:

- any path under `SPEC/game/**`
- any path under `SPEC/ui/**`
- any of these allowlisted files:
  - `SPEC/program/orders.md`
  - `SPEC/program/turn-resolution-phases.md`
  - `SPEC/program/turn-resolution-phase-details.md`
  - `SPEC/program/order-engine.md`

**Advisory only** (no mandatory path trigger): every other `SPEC/program/**` path. Authors must still update the manual when the change affects what the player can do, see, or be told (see **Player UX / gameplay impact** above).

## Manual update principles

1. **Player angle** — Explain why the player uses the mechanic and how it affects winning or enjoyment; do not merely restate a rule diff.
2. **Tone and reading level** — Per `STYLE_GUIDE.md`: vizier advising a young monarch; everyday body prose a 12th-grade reader can follow; UI-engineering and genre jargon banned; archaic flourishes only in Counsel callouts.
3. **Chapter template** — Purpose; How it is done; Counsel; The other courts; Consequences; Acceptance criteria for this chapter; Sources (last `##`).
4. **Sources footer** — Last `##` is exactly `## Sources`; each bullet is one backtick-wrapped repo-relative SPEC path with no trailing prose.
5. **Draft surfaces** — Omit, or cite as `**[DRAFT]** \`SCREENID\``; never operable steps in How it is done.
6. **Screen IDs** — Cite UI by stable 8-char IDs from `SPEC/ui/screen-registry.md`.
7. **Honesty** — Document only implemented, specced behavior; no exploit min-max guides.

## PR checklist (manual-impacting)

- [ ] Player UX/gameplay impact assessed; exempt cases justified when applicable.
- [ ] Required-review paths (if any) checked against chapter `## Sources` footers.
- [ ] Affected chapters updated **or** PR body justifies non-update.
- [ ] Player-angle framing preserved; tone and reading-level contract respected.
- [ ] Draft citations use `**[DRAFT]** \`SCREENID\`` or are omitted.
